[Music]  so a few nights ago my girlfriend and I  had a couple drinks and convinced  ourselves that we needed to go down the  street to Bond for snacks we ended up  with a sort of weird grouping of 6 items  toasted sesame water crackers some  smoked mozzarella cheese chickpea chips  a dozen eggs because you always need  eggs just sweet young coconut because I  saw it near the cash register and  scallions because honey why do we get  scallions again ah well apparently  nobody knows why we got this guy's  anyway we enjoyed the snacks they were  all really good but then I happen to  look at the cheque and I realized that I  had accidentally paid for 17 federal  programs okay  not exactly but let me explain this year  the federal budget request for the  Corporation for Public Broadcasting the  organization that runs PBS NPR and over  1,400 locally owned public radio and  television stations is four hundred and  forty five million dollars using the  latest census information that comes out  to a dollar and 37 cents per American  per year or about the cost of 12 and a  half toasted sesame water crackers the  National Endowment for the Arts wants a  budget of only 150 million to help fund  art exhibitions and our education across  the country to help America imagine  itself artistically each of us has to  pay just this much smoked mozzarella  cheese per year you might be wondering  why I'm bringing all this up it's  because in the next few weeks you're  likely to see the Trump administration  proposed dramatic budget cuts to the  federal government that will seek to  privatize the Corporation for Public  Broadcasting and eliminate the National  Endowment of the Arts completely as well  as 15 other programs thanks to some good  work from Taylor pepper over at Time  magazine we know that taken together  these 17 programs will cost every  American 22 dollars and 36 cents per  year the exact cost of my late-night  snack run here's what though each cost  you individually and what they do cue  the montage music the National Endowment  for Humanities  helps fund museums colleges libraries  and things like Ken Burns awesome Civil  War documentary it will cost you the  price of just one cake minority business  development agency promotes the growth  of businesses owned and operated by  minority entrepreneurs it costs everyone  just 11 cents or this many chopped  scallions you can fund the economic  development administration an  organization that supplies regional and  local businesses with the infrastructure  they need to compete in the global  market for 20% of the water in this  coconut for the cost of six water  crackers with cheese you can support the  international trade administration which  helps enforce trade law for US companies  for 20% of one bag of chickpea chips  you'll fund the manufacturing extension  partnership which is dedicated to  strengthening small and medium sized  manufacturers for 17% more chickpea  chips you'll fund the office of violence  against women which oversees programs  across the country that reduced domestic  violence and sexual assaults the Legal  Services Corporation helps poor  Americans afford legal services that'll  cost you just 3 eggs fried plus some  scallions the Civil Rights Division of  the Justice Department vise  discrimination and protects voting  rights that'll cost you just a couple  shots of coconut water plus some  scallions to fund the UN  Intergovernmental Panel on Climate  Change which compiles the latest  scientific data on global warming you  have to throw in just this much of a  chickpea chip the office of electricity  deliverability and energy reliability  invests in making our energy grid more  stable and secure it costs all the  scallions the scallions are really cheap  and finally the office of energy  efficiency and renewable energy aids  efforts to transition America to a clean  energy economy it's the most expensive  of the bunch yet it only costs the price  of one box of water crackers and one bag  of chips the blueprint for these cuts  comes from a paper put out by the  Heritage Foundation a conservative think  tank that has long argued for  eliminating federal programs as a way to  reduce our twenty trillion dollar  national debt but the problem is that  altogether these programs are asking for  only 7.3 billion dollars which is 1% of  the non-defense discretionary spending  that our government does  fully half of discretionary spending  goes to the military something that the  Trump administration is not likely to  slash all that much and in total all  discretionary spending makes up only 31  percent of the federal budget the rest  goes to Social Security Medicare  Medicaid entitlements that Trump has  also vowed not to touch  in other words privatizing or  eliminating these 17 programs is really  only a symbolic gesture that won't do  much of anything the good news is that  this is a fight that should be pretty  easy to win if you're willing to spend  drunkenly or not 22 dollars and 36 cents  on these 17 programs call your  Congressman and say so and if they want  to know why you think privatizing PBS or  killing the National Endowment of the  Arts is a bunch of [ __ ] feel free to  send them this video  [Music]  playing everybody thanks for watching  nerdfighter t-shirt still available at  dftba calm send me a picture if you've  got one anyway thanks the crunchyroll  for sponsoring this episode if you don't  know crunchyroll is like the Netflix of  anime it's really cool it's got  thousands of titles all HD and if  something air is in Japan it's going to  be on crunchyroll an hour later so you  can see the latest stuff ways animes  stuff coming out of Japan on crunchyroll  I want to recommend Cowboy Bebop  which is in my opinion a work of art and  if you find out that crunchyroll.com  collection nerdwriter  you get a free 30-day trial which would  allow you to watch that show and I think  that you would really like it anyway  I'll see you guys next Wednesday and  thanks again for watching

